Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?perf=20phase=2011=20patch=200115=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?engine-side=20idle-pause=20activation=20(OPL3)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DOS-PORT (patch 0115, Phase 11 iter J). Engine-side activation of the
SDL-side idle-pause helper introduced by sdl-engine slots 0037 + 0038.
The SDL helper defaults OFF; engine flips it ON via
SDL_DOSAudioSetIdlePauseEnabled(true) ONLY when the resolved music
backend is OPL3 — hardware-offload synth that does not need a
continuous DMA stream, so the DSP can be paused between Pixtone SFX
bursts to recover ~12 ms / flip of IRQ-5 wall-clock per Phase 10
design (PHASE10-DESIGN.md § E).

Why OPL3-only (not Organya, not WB-yet):
  Organya is a continuous PCM stream — pausing the DSP would gap the
  music. WaveBlaster idle-pause is a one-line follow-up if/when a WB
  iter is run but iter J's brief is OPL3-only so this patch ships
  literal-OPL3-only. Per silent_narrow_pattern.md the brief's exact
  wording is honored; broadening to WB+OPL3 is queued as a separate
  small patch when the WB iter happens.

Activation point:
  AFTER the existing backend-resolution switch in SoundManager::init
  (lines ~421-464 — auto_select chain may have rolled the enum back
  from wb to opl3 to organya, so the FINAL g_p10_audio_backend_active
  is what we read here). AFTER SDL_DOSAudioRegisterIdlePauseCallback
  so the callback is in place before the SDL-side mechanism activates.
  BEFORE the music-dir + preload + reload scan that runs after.

Killswitch:
  SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_IDLE_PAUSE=0 strict-match (only literal "0"
  disables). Default = enabled when backend == OPL3. Mirrors
  patch 0093's killswitch convention. Per
  env_vars_document_in_user_docs.md: documented in docs/BOOT.md under
  the user-facing / fallback section alongside other Phase 11 iter-J
  knobs.

Three log lines (one fires per init based on state):
  "Sound system: idle-pause-activated (patch 0115; backend=opl3; ...)"
    — default ON path (backend qualifies + killswitch off)
  "Sound system: idle-pause skipped (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_IDLE_PAUSE=0
   killswitch active; backend=opl3 would otherwise qualify). ..."
    — killswitch on, backend qualified
  "Sound system: idle-pause skipped (backend={} does not qualify; ...)"
    — backend is organya/wb/tracker/none

Cross-vendor coordination:
  Forward-decl SDL_DOSAudioSetIdlePauseEnabled added to the existing
  extern "C" block at SoundManager.cpp top (alongside the existing
  SDL_DOSAudioRegisterIdlePauseCallback decl from patch 0100).
  Linker resolves cross-vendor at combined-build time; standalone
  build of this patch alone fails unless sdl-engine's 0037+ lands
  alongside, which is the expected combined-review pattern per
  W22A precedent.

Slot 0116 SAMPLE_FRAMES knob — DEFERRED to iter K (W13.5 reconciliation):
  The iter J task brief originally proposed bundling slot 0116 — set
  SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DEVICE_SAMPLE_FRAMES=2048 to halve the IRQ-5 rate;
  predicted -6 to -11 ms / flip per FPS-DEEPDIVE § 10.C. STOPPED-and-
  acked the team-lead before authoring (per silent_narrow_pattern.md +
  force_options_on_deviations.md) because two pre-existing tree facts
  contradict the brief's prediction:

    1. Slot 0066's W13.5 experiment (real-HW PODP 5V83) measured
       SAMPLE_FRAMES=512 vs 1024 vs 2048 as 86 ms vs ~99 ms vs ~99 ms
       per flip — so 2048 was a +13 ms REGRESSION on this machine.
       Per-chunk cost scales with chunk size; the comment block at
       SoundManager.cpp:267 attributes this to L1 cache pressure
       (P54C 8 KB D-cache thrashes against an 8 KB chunk memcpy).
       Net: brief predicted -6 to -11 ms gain; existing measurement
       said +13 ms regression — a -19 to -24 ms gap between
       prediction and data, too large to ship without reconciliation
       per measurements_above_prediction_are_red_flags.md.

    2. Slot 0093's Tier-2 default-ON config already pins
       SAMPLE_FRAMES=256 via SDL_HINT_OVERRIDE priority — the
       wave-21 Lever G mechanism that halves IRQ rate to 43 Hz at
       11025 mono. Slot 0116 with normal priority would lose to the
       OVERRIDE; with OVERRIDE priority would directly fight Lever G.

  Decision (team-lead, Option 4): defer slot 0116 to iter K pending
  iter-J AUDBUF probe data. The AUDBUF probe (probe-engineer's lane)
  maps the cost curve at multiple buffer sizes; iter K's slot becomes
  data-driven — the sweet spot may not be 2048 (could be 384, 512,
  etc.). Per probe_first_optimization.md.

  Future-claude reading this patch series: if you're considering
  bumping SAMPLE_FRAMES on this hardware, look at AUDBUF probe data
  first AND reconcile against the W13.5 measurement embedded in
  SoundManager.cpp:262-274. The "bigger buffer = always better"
  intuition does not hold on PODP5V83 with INDEX8 mixer + small L1.

DOSBox-X smoke (build-validated):
  build SHA: 40719b95b1cbde673f9275401032f9be77649087a29eb2875373b8fbfaae1000
  strings markers verified embedded in binary:
    - "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_IDLE_PAUSE"
    - "Sound system: idle-pause-activated (patch 0115; ...)"
    - "Sound system: idle-pause skipped (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_IDLE_PAUSE=0
       killswitch active; ...)"
    - "Sound system: idle-pause skipped (backend={} does not qualify;
       ...)"
  Real-HW iter J PLAY1 (OPL3 backend) is the load-bearing measurement
  gate per dosbox_not_perf_proxy.md.

Out of scope (per silent_narrow_pattern.md scope discipline):
  - WB-backend extension (would be a one-line addition to the
    backend_qualifies disjunction; deferred until a WB iter is run)
  - SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_IDLE_PAUSE_FORCE=1 to force-enable on
    non-qualifying backends (would gap Organya music; not useful)
  - Per-stage idle-pause threshold tuning (the sdl-engine 0037+
    helpers handle this; engine just toggles the gate)
  - SAMPLE_FRAMES knob (slot 0116; deferred to iter K — see W13.5
    reconciliation above)

